---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Clouds from '../components/Clouds.astro';
import '../styles/note.css';

const DESCRIPTION =
    'What data this site collects, what I use it for, who else sees it, ' +
    'and how to get it deleted.';
---

<Layout lang='en' title='Privacy Policy — Renzo Tincopa' description={DESCRIPTION}>
    <div class='relative w-full bg-sunset min-h-dvh flex flex-col'>
        <Clouds perZone={3} />
        <section class='relative z-10 flex-1 py-12 md:py-16'>
            <h1 class='has-dots mb-6 text-center'>Privacy Policy</h1>
            <article class='note-card'>
                <div class='note'>
                    <p>
                        This site asks for very little and uses it for one thing:
                        replying to you. Here are the rules, short and without fine
                        print. Last updated: <strong>October 30, 2026</strong>.
                    </p>

                    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
                    <p>
                        Renzo Tincopa, an individual based in Urubamba, Cusco, Peru.
                        For anything about your data, message me on
                        <a href='https://t.me/tinconomad' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer'
                            >Telegram: @tinconomad</a
                        >.
                    </p>

                    <h2>What I collect</h2>
                    <p>Only what you write yourself, in two forms:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Free review</strong> (<a href='/diagnostico-gratis'
                                >/diagnostico-gratis</a
                            >): name or nickname, what system you run, what it is
                            costing you, the channel you prefer for contact, and
                            the detail for that channel (phone, email or handle).
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Contact form</strong> (the "Let's build
                            together" button): name, email or Telegram, project
                            type, budget range, priorities and your message.
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>
                        And the recommendations published in the Reviews section,
                        explained further down. No passwords, no card numbers, no
                        sensitive data. If you send them anyway, I delete them.
                    </p>

                    <h2>Why I use it</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li>To reply and give you the review or quote you asked for.</li>
                        <li>To run the project, if we end up working together.</li>
                        <li>
                            To tell your case publicly as an example — only if you
                            tick that box in the free review form, and without
                            your name unless you say otherwise.
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>
                        Nothing else. No mailing list, no ads, no selling or renting
                        data, and no automated decisions about you.
                    </p>

                    <h2>Legal basis</h2>
                    <p>
                        Your consent. Sending a form is your permission, and you can
                        take it back whenever you want.
                    </p>

                    <h2>Who else sees it</h2>
                    <p>
                        Your data passes through three hands, and none of them use it
                        for their own purposes:
                    </p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Web3Forms</strong> (<a
                                href='https://web3forms.com/privacy'
                                target='_blank'
                                rel='noopener noreferrer'>web3forms.com/privacy</a
                            >): receives the form and forwards it to my email. It
                            keeps a copy in its dashboard under its own policy.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Cloudflare</strong>: serves the site and keeps
                            technical logs (IP address, date, page) for security and
                            uptime.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <strong>My email provider</strong>: where the forwarded
                            message lands.
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>No analytics, no social pixels, no advertising.</p>

                    <h2>How long I keep it</h2>
                    <p>
                        One year from your last message if nothing moves forward;
                        after that I delete it. If we work together, for the length
                        of the project plus whatever the law makes me keep
                        (accounting records, for example). Recommendations stay up
                        until you ask me to take them down.
                    </p>

                    <h2>Cookies</h2>
                    <p>
                        One: <code>access</code>. It opens a private note without
                        asking for the password on every page. It is technical,
                        lasts 7 days and tracks nothing. That is why there is no
                        cookie banner here.
                    </p>

                    <h2>Your rights</h2>
                    <p>
                        You can ask me to show you what I have, correct it, delete
                        it, stop using it, or take back your consent. Message me on
                        Telegram and tell me what you need.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        If you are not happy with my answer, you can go to the
                        National Authority for Personal Data Protection (ANPD) at
                        the Ministry of Justice and Human Rights of Peru.
                    </p>

                    <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
                    <p>This is a commitment, not a vague gesture.</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>
                            Message me on <a
                                href='https://t.me/tinconomad'
                                target='_blank'
                                rel='noopener noreferrer'>Telegram</a
                            >
                            with the word "data" and tell me what to remove.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            Within <strong>7 business days</strong> I send
                            you an email confirming what I deleted and on what
                            date. Give me an email address in the chat, and that
                            email is your receipt.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            If your name is in a recommendation or a published
                            case, it comes off the site the same day. Search
                            engines and saved copies can take a few days to catch
                            up; that part is out of my hands.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            The only thing I keep is what the law makes me keep,
                            such as accounting records.
                        </li>
                    </ul>

                    <h2>Recommendations</h2>
                    <p>
                        The reviews in the Reviews section are recommendations
                        people left me on LinkedIn. I republish the name, role and
                        profile link that came with each recommendation. If you
                        delete your recommendation on LinkedIn, or simply change
                        your mind, message me on Telegram and it comes off the
                        site the same day.
                    </p>

                    <h2>Minors</h2>
                    <p>
                        This site is for people hiring services. I do not knowingly
                        collect data from minors. If you think I kept data from a
                        minor, tell me and I delete it.
                    </p>

                    <h2>Changes</h2>
                    <p>
                        If something changes, I update the date at the top. The
                        version published here is the one that counts.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </article>
        </section>
    </div>
    <div class='sunset-fade'></div>
</Layout>
